<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:45Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Rising emissions and temperatures: The cost of Trump's climate retreat is now clear</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04ae7f3fad1c0caf0a80450ac54aef106e9f63040d535ce0a494819fbf04e7a1</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T05:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-cost-of-trump-s-climate-retreat-is-now-clear/a-79714915--c58ce7a39bf5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-cost-of-trump-s-climate-retreat-is-now-clear/a-79714915?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The world is set to breach the critical 1.5-degree temperature limit, with Donald Trump's US withdrawal from climate action worsening the outlook, according to a UN report. But there is a small silver lining.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Elon Musk ordered a slowdown of Starlink in Ukraine — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9edbb28df3a8f937ef2e3aab46137d307df19ff758cdf530500960aeea857c7d</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T03:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elon-musk-ordered-a-slowdown-of-starlink-in-ukraine-report/a-79718899--f41ab1e64a12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elon-musk-ordered-a-slowdown-of-starlink-in-ukraine-report/a-79718899?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk "capped the speeds at which Ukrainian hardware could stay connected to the satellite-based network," the Wall Street Journal reported.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK fighter jets to protect Saudi Arabia from Houthi attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c31e1f3208c295c807be78f9e3604c1e79ac85d0f69fe456fdaa5cb51d72b2bc</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T01:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-fighter-jets-to-protect-saudi-arabia-from-houthi-attacks/a-79718467--d87226c03f76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-fighter-jets-to-protect-saudi-arabia-from-houthi-attacks/a-79718467?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UK is sending military support to Saudi Arabia as Iran-aligned Houthi rebels launch repeated attacks on the kingdom.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Portugal housing protests continue after police clear camps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b8bcae72d29418c824c47ee5d2322459dcff03efafabf8d9f551fc08995bb9d</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T23:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/portugal-housing-protests-continue-after-police-clear-camps/a-79717904--9c24875c39a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/portugal-housing-protests-continue-after-police-clear-camps/a-79717904?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators vow to continue their campaign to call for affordable housing in Portugal after police cleared tent camps and arrested at least 55 people.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>AfD's Alice Weidel to unveil plan to cut EU powers — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77cd17bc3ebf174d77dec35b915f69778f7e94756b8bc5caaaaacaa6c099c7a0</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T22:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-s-alice-weidel-to-unveil-plan-to-cut-eu-powers-report/a-79717944--20fa5b0134f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-s-alice-weidel-to-unveil-plan-to-cut-eu-powers-report/a-79717944?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD will propose slashing powers of the European Union when it presents its policy paper on Wednesday, Politico reports.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Zelenskyy visits Norway amid Trump White House tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7aaca452498dfc81b0eeae2b6e309851bc0f5d0c2219c6344f4b198effd8bfac</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-visits-norway-amid-trump-white-house-tensions/a-79717354--f26d4c094394.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-visits-norway-amid-trump-white-house-tensions/a-79717354?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy met with Norwegian and Finnish leaders in Oslo and held talks with Trump envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner. Trump is pressuring Zelenskyy to "make a deal" with Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case, in capital Abuja</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41a924a3530342fad3bcc6ddbb6148ab040bc00137140ecf33f2fcdd8af632f1</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377--c6985b1c776f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigeria has reported its first known case of Ebola during Africa's latest outbreak originating in the DRC. Health Minister Muhammad Ali Pate said the patient was a woman who had recently flown to Abuja from Uganda.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Lebanon faces uncertainty as UNIFIL mandate nears end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35fb078ebe9ddaeb59b1f641f3995fc34c9bb1774e1a27cf54a088137987a4c2</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491--a12453a4b744.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As UN peacekeeping forces prepare to withdraw from Lebanon, Israel remains present and Hezbollah is still armed. A new EU support mission aims to strengthen Lebanon's army, but will not replace UN peacekeepers.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan drone strike kills around 150 in Abyei market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50e537b6b8e89dd6183123d07932979e8af4d8fccbf59a465357a3b68a8d585e</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587--6d5e17c39f6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A drone strike hit a market in the Abyei border region disputed by Sudan and South Sudan and killed dozens. The drone caused a large fire when it hit a fuel depot. South Sudanese officials blamed Sudan's military.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory, says new report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef9309c97e160d17723f00857b017349de5a4338f2ec639e7eecd624be419794</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877--a509ee21abbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New EU plan for Arctic warily eyes influence of Russia, US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:012c68830a841c543fa2f0918f0d4e964d1a8eec83fd1a90746194a164e2d4dd</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219--7030ab283919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU unveiled its priorities in the Arctic as it vies with Russia, China and the US for influence. EU foreign affairs chief Kaja Kallas said drone incursions, GPS jamming and cable sabotage undermine Arctic security.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France plans 'massive' weekend police surge amid protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:070d4723647b148e30e90d02ef92e806505f5df695e2d723b8f206c3fdc6eeeb</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-plans-massive-weekend-police-surge-amid-protests/live-79707186--61242b391ca9.html" type="text/htm